//
// Expected: c1 at one session and at two.
//
// Alice keeps the result of an ASSERT and uses it as a key. An ASSERT stores
// the assertion term itself, and every input of this one is public, so the
// attacker builds ASSERT(x, x) as Alice did and opens `e`. The engine once
// refused to let the attacker build any ASSERT, while Alice could hold one.
// core_assert_value_private.vp is the counterweight.
attacker[passive]
principal Alice[
	knows public x
	generates sec
	h = ASSERT(x, x)
	e = ENC(h, sec)
]
Alice -> Bob: e
principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(e)
]
queries[
	confidentiality? sec
]
